WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.260
So you'd like to add a shoulder
slope to your pattern?

2
00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:06.980
Or maybe you want to shape
the top of a pocket?

3
00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:12.940
Use the Knit It Now Slope tool to
calculate the shaping over a short slope.

4
00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:15.060
Now, this is a variation of the Magic

5
00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:21.100
Formula to use when you're shaping
over more stitches than rows.

6
00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:23.440
Start by choosing if your measurement is

7
00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:27.860
in inches, centimeters
or stitches and rows.

8
00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:37.860
Then enter your gauge,
enter the starting width and depth

9
00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:42.180
and the tool will give you
precise knitting instructions.

10
00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:44.620
Use the Knit it Now Slope Tool to quickly

11
00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:48.880
calculate the shaping over more stitches
than rows, just like in a shoulder slope.

